<title>USA: Digital Biometrics names new CEO.</title>
<headline>Digital Biometrics names new CEO.</headline>
<dateline>MINNETONKA, Minn. 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Digital Biometrics Inc said James Granger was named president and chief executive effective immediately.</p>
<p>The maker of live-scan fingerprint products and player tracking systems for the gaming industry said Granger comes from ADC Telecommunications Inc, where he was president of the access platforms systems division.</p>
<p>He succeeds Jack Klingert, who was chief executive for 10 years and is retiring.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787))</p>
